I will post properly on this topic when the debate has died down a
bit. In the meantime, I should clarify.

I intended {pi ro xoi} to = {jaa} and {pi no xoi} to = {na}.
I wasn't saying that there is at present anything unsayable without
{xoi}: I recognize that circumlocutions with {jei} and other devices
are possible. But equally, so could we do without {na} and {jaa} and
make do with {jei}. But that we would find too cumbersome. So it's
on grounds of convenience that I felt {xoi} to be motivated.

It is my impression that this is the understanding Jorge formed of
my proposal.

