My giuste, which is not bang up to date, has:

   clani  long    x1 is long in dimension/direction x2 (default
   longest dimens.) by meas. stand. x3;

Mind you, I would rather you were right. I find all these antonymous
gismu pairs like clani/tordu to be antipathetic - I'd much rather
discard tordu, make clani mean "has length" and say "mutce clani"
and "milxe clani" for long and short. The present noisome system
is (ill) motivated by the objectionable need to be culturally neutral.

